WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.670
- So one interesting philosophical point

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.970
in quantum mechanics bring up is the,

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:07.480
that you talk about the distinction

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:12.343
between the world as it is and
the world as we observe it.

00:00:13.417 --> 00:00:17.190
So, staying at the human
level for a second.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:19.160
How big is the gap between

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.250
what our perception
system allows us to see

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:26.294
and the world as is is
outside our mind's eye,

00:00:26.294 --> 00:00:29.260
sort of, not at the
quantum mechanical level

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:33.560
but as just our, these
particular tools we have

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.230
which is a few senses and
our cognitive abilities

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:38.030
to process those senses?

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:39.967
- Well, that last phrase,

00:00:39.967 --> 00:00:41.960
"Having the cognitive
abilities to process them."

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.470
carries a lot, right?

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:47.110
I mean there is our sort
of intuitive understanding

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:48.470
of the world.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:50.580
You don't need to teach
people about gravity

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.300
for them to know that apples
fall from trees, right?

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.410
That's something that we
figure out pretty quickly.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.470
Object permanence, things like that.

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:58.990
The three-dimensionality of space,

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:01.730
even if we don't have the
mathematical language to say that,

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:03.790
we kind of know that it's true.

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:08.090
On the other hand, no one opens
their eyes and sees atoms.

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:10.250
Or molecules, or cells for that matter,

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.950
forget about quantum mechanics.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:15.840
So, but we got there,
we got to understanding

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.460
that there are atoms and cells,

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.286
using the combination of our senses

00:01:20.286 --> 00:01:22.810
and our cognitive capacities.

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:26.250
So adding the ability of
our cognitive capacities

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.800
to our senses is adding an enormous amount

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.450
and I don't think that it
is a hard and fast boundary.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.630
You know if you believe in cells,

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:35.200
if you believe that we
can understand those,

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.850
then there's no reason
you believe we can't,

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:39.950
believe in quantum mechanics just as well.

